# xtdl-values-example: a FICTIONAL format, invented only for this example: a
# 27-byte binary report that shows the value transforms of engine-spec 0.15
# (octal digits, sign and magnitude, an integer scale, a 6-bit character set
# and a scaled IEEE float), and `absent` on a sign-and-magnitude field. Layout: pack.md.
format        xtdl-values-example
version       0.2.0
distribution  controlled
source        "invented for this example; no external document"
uses          xtdl
wire          bits
word_bytes    1
bit_order     msb

field  uid                  0:0:15     octal
field  lat                  0:15:25    smscale:1/100000  absent 16777216
field  lon                  0:40:26    smscale:1/100000
field  time_ms              0:66:56    uiscale:1/1000
field  callsign             0:122:54   chars:icao6
field  speed_ms             0:176:32   f32scale:1/10
field  xtdl.lane_offset_m   0:208:8    smag
